-*- markdown -*-
% ntfy, notification

# publish a simple message to a topic
```shell
ntfy publish <topic> <message>
```

# publish with a title
```shell
ntfy publish -t <title> <topic> <message>
```

# publish with priority (1=min, 2=low, 3=default, 4=high, 5=max)
```shell
ntfy publish -p <priority> <topic> <message>
```

# publish with tags / emojis (comma separated)
```shell
ntfy publish --tags <tags> <topic> <message>
```

# publish with a click URL (opens when notification is tapped)
```shell
ntfy publish --click <url> <topic> <message>
```

# publish with a file attachment
```shell
ntfy publish --file <path> <topic> <message>
```

# publish message body from stdin
```shell
echo <message> | ntfy publish <topic>
```

# schedule a message at a specific time (e.g. 8:30am, 10s, 1h)
```shell
ntfy publish --at <time> <topic> <message>
```

# run a command and notify when it finishes
```shell
ntfy publish --wait-cmd <topic> <command>
```

# wait for a PID to exit then notify
```shell
ntfy publish --wait-pid <pid> <topic>
```

# publish with access token authentication
```shell
ntfy publish -k <token> <topic> <message>
```

# publish with username:password authentication
```shell
ntfy publish -u <user:pass> <topic> <message>
```

# subscribe to a topic (stream messages to stdout)
```shell
ntfy subscribe <topic>
```

# subscribe and output messages as JSON
```shell
ntfy subscribe --poll <topic>
```
